    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-8988",
      "problem": "The radius of the base of a right cylinder is $3 \\: \\textrm{m}$ and its height is $6 \\: \\textrm{m}.$ Find the lateral surface area of the cylinder.",
      "worked_solution": "We can calculate the lateral surface area of a cylinder using the formula\n\n$$\nS_L = 2\\pi r h,\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the radius and $h$ is the height of the cylinder.\n\nSubstituting $r=3 \\,\\textrm{m}$ and $h=6 \\,\\textrm{m}$ into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{L} & =2\\pi (3)(6)=36\\pi \\,{\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
